@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Cancellation Policy";
}

<div class="container d-flex justify-content-center" style="min-height: 50vh;">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div>
            <div style="color: white; user-select: none;">
                <a>_________________________________________________________________________________________</a>
            </div>
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                <a class="little-white-button" asp-controller="home" asp-action="index" style="text-decoration: none; width: 90px;">
                    <div class="text-content fs-6 px-2 fw-bold text-center">
                        <div>< Back</div>
                    </div>
                </a>
                <div class="text-center" style="flex-grow: 1;">
                    <h2>Cancellation Policy</h2>
                </div>
                <div style="width: 100px;"></div>
            </div>
            <hr />
            <div style="font-size: 18px; max-width: 800px; text-align:justify;">
                <p>We understand that unforeseen circumstances may arise, requiring you to cancel or reschedule an appointment. However, to ensure efficient scheduling and availability for all patients, we have implemented the following cancellation policy:</p>

                <p><strong>The No-Show Fee has been implemented on our website.</strong> This measure allows healthcare facilities, health services, medical centers, and independent healthcare professionals to apply a penalty in the following cases:</p>

                <ul>
                    <li>Failure to attend a scheduled appointment without prior notice;</li>
                    <li>Cancellation of an appointment without providing reasonable advance notice*.</li>
                </ul>

                <p>However, this measure is subject to specific regulations. The No-Show Fee will not be applied if the absence or late cancellation is justified by:</p>

                <ul>
                    <li>A compelling personal or family reason;</li>
                    <li>A health condition preventing attendance at the medical appointment.</li>
                </ul>

                <p style="font-size: 15px"><em>*The cancellation notice period is specific to each practitioner. It may vary between 6 hours and 30 minutes before an appointment. For more information, please pay close attention when scheduling your appointment, as the applicable cancellation notice period will be communicated to you.</em></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>